From: hashtagbasit
Subject: power: supply: qcom_battmgr: real power and a time to full on SM8550-family firmware

On a Pocket FIT (SM8650) the firmware's battery power reading is stale: it
sat at 99.18 W while the battery took 19.7 W (2.3 A at 8.6 V), and it has
no time-to-full estimate at all (-1). UPower derives the charge rate from
power_now and Steam shows "??" for the time until charged.

For the SM8550 variant:
- power_now is the battery's own current times its voltage.
- time_to_full_avg, when the firmware has none and the battery is charging,
  is the charge still to go (up to the charge limit when one is set, since
  that is when charging stops) over the charging current.

---
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_battmgr.c
@@ -600,6 +600,17 @@
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_POWER_NOW:
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.power_now;
+		/*
+		 * The SM8550-family firmware's power reading goes stale: a Pocket
+		 * FIT reported a fixed 99.18 W while its battery took 19.7 W, and
+		 * UPower (and Steam through it) take the charge and drain rate
+		 * from here. Report the battery's own current times voltage.
+		 */
+		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550 && battmgr->status.voltage_now) {
+			s64 ua = abs(battmgr->status.current_now);
+
+			val->intval = (int)div_s64(ua * battmgr->status.voltage_now, 1000000);
+		}
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_FULL_DESIGN:
 		if (unit != QCOM_BATTMGR_UNIT_mAh)
@@ -663,6 +674,25 @@
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_TIME_TO_FULL_AVG:
 		val->intval = battmgr->status.charge_time;
+		/*
+		 * This firmware has no estimate (-1), so Steam shows "??" while
+		 * charging. Estimate it from the charge still to go and the
+		 * charging current, up to the charge limit when one is set: that
+		 * is when charging stops.
+		 */
+		if (battmgr->variant == QCOM_BATTMGR_SM8550 &&
+		    (int)battmgr->status.charge_time <= 0 &&
+		    battmgr->status.status == POWER_SUPPLY_STATUS_CHARGING &&
+		    battmgr->status.current_now > 0) {
+			u64 target = battmgr->info.last_full_capacity;
+			unsigned int end = battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_end;
+
+			if (end > 0 && end < 100)
+				target = div_u64(target * end, 100);
+			val->intval = target > battmgr->status.capacity ?
+				(int)div_u64((target - battmgr->status.capacity) * 3600,
+					     battmgr->status.current_now) : 0;
+		}
 		break;
 	case POWER_SUPPLY_PROP_CHARGE_CONTROL_START_THRESHOLD:
 		val->intval = battmgr->info.charge_ctrl_start;
